BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poetry Lives in October 2026 — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, 
 California
DTSTART:20261027T000000
DTEND:20261028T000000
UID:1fcfc233772cf51741eb6dbd2da7fca7@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Poetry Lives! October 27th\n\n  \n    \n      \n      from $0.
 00\n    \n  \n\nEvery Fourth Tuesday: October 27th 6:00-7:00pm: Spoken Wor
 d Workshop 7:15-8:30pm: Open Mic Open to All$5/10/15/20 Sliding Scale for 
 Workshop Join us for an evening of spoken word poetry here at the Sebastop
 ol Center for the Arts! Students of all walks of life\, abilities\, and ex
 perience writing poetry\, or spoken word poetry\, are encouraged to join. 
 Students will engage in a freewrite\, poetry reading\, discussion\, and st
 ructured writing with a voluntary shareout. After the one hour workshop\, 
 Poetry Lives! will act as an Open Mic night open to all to read their comp
 leted\, or previously completed\, poems. To register for the Open Mic onl
 y\, please select Open Mic Only below! All workshop registrations include 
 registration to the open mic as well. Poetry Lives! is a monthly poetry wo
 rkshop and open mic series that aims to create a space for anyone and ever
 yone to come\, learn more about poetic craft\, and share their poetry. The
  event starts with a facilitated hour-long workshop dedicated to learning 
 craft elements\, discovering new poets\, and generating new work. Once the
  workshop concludes\, we will hold a hosted open mic for anyone who wishes
  to share. It is not mandatory to participate in the workshop to be a part
  of the open mic or vice versa. This event is all ages\, but that doesn't 
 necessarily mean family-friendly\, as poets are known to cover mature and 
 adult topics from time to time. About the Poet: Jordan Ranft (He/Him) is 
 a writer and therapist from Northern California. He has been nominated for
  a Pushcart and Best of the Net. His poetry has been published or is forth
 coming in Boulevard Magazine\, Frontier Poetry\, Poetry Online\, Bear Revi
 ew\, Iron Horse Literary Review\, and elsewhere. His first chapbook\, Said
  the Worms\, was published in June 2023 by Wrong Publishing. He is current
 ly working on a second chapbook and full-length collection. Instagram: @Jo
 rdan_Ranft // @poetrylivessonoma\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  Workshop
 :\n                \n\n\n\n                      Select Workshop\n        
             \n$5.00\n$10.00\n$15.00\n$20.00\nOpen Mic Only\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
