DESCRIPTION:Out of Stock\n      \n    \n\n\n\n\n\nQuiet Light: Watercolor 
 Basics\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $170.00\n        \n      \
 n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, November 7th\, 2026 10AM - 4PMSettle into the quie
 t beauty of late fall with a day of watercolor inspired bySonoma County in
  November—natural forms gathered from the season—pomegranates\, mushro
 oms\, lichen\, branches\, turning leaves\, seed pods\,and olives all broug
 ht into the classroom for observation and inspiration.The focus is on the 
 contrast of rich\, saturated color and varied texture—fiery maples\, gol
 ds\, and russets alongside muted stems\, weathered bark\,and softer\, fadi
 ng tones.Learn basic watercolor techniques including wet-on-wet painting\,
  controlledwashes\, layering\, color mixing\, and creating texture\, while
  building strongcompositions using color\, light\, and form. Guided discus
 sions explore theessential elements of visual art to help you create expre
 ssive\, individualwork.All materials provided. Space limited to 12 student
 s.Discussion break at 12:30 p.m. Please bring a brown bag lunch.About the 
 Instructor: Lynn Zachreson studied art at the University of Minnesota and 
 San Jose State University—Painting\, Printmaking: BA Fine Art. She has e
 xperience teaching all ages: Watercolor painting skills\, 30+ years\, Wate
 rcolor figure painting 20+ years\, and Fine Art Basics with Mixed Media 20
 + years. Lynn enjoys spending her time painting\, teaching\, long distance
  hiking\, and gardening. View Lynn’s art here: https://lynnzachresonart.
 com/\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            Reserve Your Spot
