SUMMARY:Still Life in Acrylic (Natural Earth Paint\, Plastic-Free Acrylic)
  — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261108T000000
DTEND:20261109T000000
UID:2f97d801b6d14088705e3e13ac857ee6@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Still Life in Acrylic (Natural Earth Paint\, Plastic-Free Acry
 lic)\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $67.00\n        \n      \n  
   \n  \n\nMuted Still Life in Acrylic (Natural Earth Paint\, Plastic-Free 
 Acrylic) Date: Sunday\, November 8th\, 2026Time: 10:00am-2:00pm Where: Seb
 astopol Center for the Arts is located at 282 South High Street in Sebasto
 pol\, CA. Details regarding class room and directions will be sent to stud
 ents 24 hours before the class beings. Price: $55.00 + $12.00 Materials Fe
 e = $67.00 Attendance Price Students: This class is restricted to a maximu
 m of 12 students. Register while you can! If this class is sold out\, plea
 se click where it says ‘sold out’  to join the waitlist! Class Descrip
 tion: In this introductory class\, you will learn basic painting technique
 s of composition\, value blocking\, and color mixing. Students will be cre
 ating a single 8x10 still life from start to finish\, painting citrus frui
 t with a blue cup. Students will learn to observe shapes and their relatio
 nship to space\, utilize tone and color to demonstrate depth\, light\, and
  shadow\, and how to complete an acrylic painting. This class is perfect 
 for beginners\, and painters of all skill-levels\, looking to hone in thei
 r acrylic painting skills. This class focuses on utilizing eco-friendly m
 aterials and uses non-toxic\, plastic free Natural Earth Paint\, which is 
 safe to wash down your drain without impacting the Earth! About the Teach
 er: Amy Sundahl is a painter and visual artist. She grew up surrounded by 
 the green hills of Northern California. The palette of blue sky\, green an
 d gold hills\, grey coastal cliffs\, and burnt orange redwoods still infor
 m her work today. Amy began to be influenced by the abstract shapes and la
 rge plains of the city scape. These influences show up in structured space
 s and textures in her work. To Amy\, everyday life is rich in color and me
 aning. Her approach comes with curiosity and humor. Amy’s work has been 
 compared to American artists such as Edward Hopper\, Wayne Thiebaud\, and 
 Richard Diebenkorn. Amy currently lives in Long Beach\, CA. Click here to 
 learn more about Amy on her website! Check out her Instagram @amy_sundahl.
  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n       
    \n            Register
